      {
        "bug_id": "BUG-002",
        "title": "OFF_BY_ONE_NULL_WRITE_IN_CREATE_COOKIE",
        "root_cause": {
          "type": "Size Calculation Error",
          "description": "In create_cookie, after read(0, buf, msg_length), the code checks if buf[read_ret] == '\\n' and if so writes buf[read_ret] = '\\0'. When read() returns exactly msg_length bytes (full buffer, no newline in last position), the index read_ret equals msg_length, which is one byte past the end of the calloc(msg_length, 1) allocation. The NUL write at buf[msg_length] corrupts the first byte beyond the allocated buffer."
